# Verified assets must be byte-exact on every platform.
#
# ``kvmhub/video/client_v2.verify_bundle()`` compares each file's SHA-256 with
# the pinned manifest, and that digest *is* the client build identity. A Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF, which changes both the
# byte count and the digest, so the bundle looks tampered with and every lane
# session is refused with pipeline_version_unavailable. Checking these paths out
# verbatim keeps the identity meaningful off Linux.
kvmhub/static/novnc-v2/** -text
frontend/vendor/** -text

# Same rule, same failure mode: ``kvmhub/transcode/registry.PLUGINS`` locks the
# SHA-256 of each plugin source, and ``PluginSpec.check_source()`` refuses the
# family when the digest differs. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout
# rewrites these files to CRLF, so every transcode family refuses to build with
# ``transcode_family_unsupported`` — on Windows only, and only after checkout,
# which is exactly the "works on my machine" shape this file exists to prevent.
kvmhub/transcode/*.py -text
